{"id": "EUVD-2026-100486", "enisaUuid": "8ab3cd8f-6bf6-3d7f-a072-0747aa2a9342", "description": "The auth0/java-jwt library may terminate a thread if it receives a JWT with a timestamp claim (exp, nbf, iat) containing an out-of-range value. The condition occurs during token parsing, prior to signature verification. Repeated requests of this nature may lead to degraded availability of the affected service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T20:08:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T15:31:55", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://trust.okta.com/security-advisories/out-of-range-timestamp-claim-handling-in-auth0-java-jwt-cve-2026-85473", "https://github.com/auth0/java-jwt/security/advisories/GHSA-cg7w-5cc2-f2xm"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-85473"], "assigner": "Okta", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "afe3a407-60fb-3a6e-afe5-d5f11aa4d1a7", "product": {"name": "java-jwt", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}, "product_version": "4.0.0 <4.6.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "84c5c10f-78d5-3c73-b4ef-ec446af60a0b", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}], "isExploited": false}